+Aegis Consulting Engagement — One‑Page Summary
+
+Objective
+- Deliver a repeatable, auditable Proof‑of‑Automation (PoA) using the Aegis platform that validates end‑to‑end capabilities: data → train → sim → HIL → formal → auditor bundle. Provide actionable gaps, KPI measurement, and a handoff package so your team can operate the flow independently.
+
+Scope
+- One representative target (controller or model) to exercise the full pipeline:
+  - Example controller: falcon-ecu-01.example.com:can0
+  - Example model: perception‑backbone v0.1 (ONNX)
+- Run stages:
+  1. Tokenize & shard (LLM path) or data packaging (perception)
+  2. Minimal sharded training smoke test (1 node / 1 GPU)
+  3. Small sim batch (2 packs) to collect failures (dry-run permitted)
+  4. Hardware RT sweeps: p99 jitter & safe‑stop proofs (signed)
+  5. HIL campaign + Apalache triage against one safety invariant
+  6. Build signed auditor bundle and submit to certifier endpoint
+
+Artifacts delivered
+- Prefilled one‑click PoA script (executes the pipeline and records timings).  
+- Prefilled GitHub Actions workflow to run the PoA on self‑hosted runners.  
+- HIL + Apalache closure script prefilled for the selected invariant.  
+- KPI dashboard template (Grafana JSON) and a sample KPI report (before/after).  
+- Evidence bundle (signed if COSIGN_KMS_URI provided) and PoA report (JSON).  
+- Short remediation list and prioritized gaps discovered during the run.
+
+Timeline (typical)
+- Day 0 (Planning): Confirm representative target, SLOs, NPU runner names, and provide credentials/placeholders for COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, S3_UPLOAD. (Owner: Platform + Controls)  
+- Day 1–3 (Provision & validation): Validate one hardened builder, validate minimal GPU node, verify runner labeling and KMS/OIDC snippets. (Owner: Infra)  
+- Day 3–7 (PoA run): Execute one‑click PoA, triage failures (HIL/Apalache), iterate quick fixes. (Owners: Controls, Perception, Infra)  
+- Day 8–10 (Report & Handoff): Deliver KPI report, auditor bundle, and a prioritized remediation list + runbook for routine execution. (Owner: Platform)
+
+Team & Owners
+- Engagement Lead / Platform: alice.platform@example.com — overall delivery, evidence packaging.  
+- Controls / HIL: carol.controls@example.com — RT sweeps, HIL runs, waveform triage.  
+- Perception / ML: dave.perception@example.com — data prep, sharded smoke, retrain triage.  
+- Infra: erin.infra@example.com — builder hardening, KMS/OIDC, GPU provisioning.  
+- Safety Officer: bob.safety@example.com — approval on safety invariant & certifier submission.
+
+Acceptance criteria
+- PoA run completes end‑to‑end and produces a signed auditor bundle (or explains why signing was skipped).  
+- RT proofs exist for the representative target with p99_ms and safe_ms values recorded.  
+- HIL + Apalache run either closes the invariant or produces triage artifacts and a remediation list.  
+- KPI report shows Time‑to‑Evidence and a before/after comparison (baseline optional).  
+- CI provenance gate (cosign + Rekor) is exercised at least once in the run.
+
+Risks & mitigations
+- Risk: Hardware unavailability — Mitigation: run dry‑run sim & smoke training, record evidence for missing hardware, schedule hardware window.  
+- Risk: Cosign/KMS not configured — Mitigation: run unsigned PoA but record manifest and include step-by-step KMS integration instructions in handoff.  
+- Risk: Long perception long‑tail — Mitigation: use small sim packs for PoA and document scaling plan for full campaigns.
+
+Handoff
+- Deliverables posted to S3 (or your artifact store) and recorded via ops.sdk.evidence_sdk.record_manifest for audit. A knowledge transfer session (2 hours) will be scheduled.
+
+Contact to start
+- Reply with representative controller/model (host:iface or model name), desired SLOs (p99_ms, safe_ms, LLM p99 latency), NPU runner hostnames, and artifact upload target (S3 or similar).
